Z||000003||fierofreek2001||04-04-2001||09:21 PM||||anyone have any thoughts on what i could do to solve this problem?<BR>thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||04-04-2001||09:26 PM||||You're EGR's not working. Check the vacuum line to it, at idle, using some thick gloves or a rag, push up on the underside of it and verify that the engine starts to stumble or dies. If it doesn't, the passages are clogged and need clean. If it does, either the EGR diaphram is torn or vacuum's not getting to it.<P>At cruise, the EGR is open and spark is added to the timing. If the EGR is not working, there is too much advance. When you floor it, the EGR closes and the added timing is removed. That's why it goes away.<P>There could be something else wrong, but 90% of the time, that's the problem unless you have the timing mis-adjusted. ||||reg||1
